Accessing Cross Account Access :

  - In cross-account access, one AWS account wants to access a resource in another AWS account.
  - The resource-owning account creates the IAM role.
  - The role contains a trust policy and a permission policy.

Example :

  - Account A contains an EC2 instance.
  - Account B contains an S3 bucket.
  - Account A wants to access the S3 bucket in Account B.

Step-by-step :

  1. Create a role in Account B, for example : CrossAccountS3AccessRole.
  2. Add a trust policy in Account B so that Account A can assume the role.
  3. Add a permission policy in Account B to allow access to the S3 bucket.
  4. In Account A, allow the EC2 instance or user to call sts:AssumeRole.
  5. STS checks the trust policy and, if valid, returns temporary credentials.
  6. The user or EC2 instance uses those temporary credentials to access the S3 bucket.

Trust policy example (Account B):

  {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Principal": {
          "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_A_ID:root"
        },
        "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  }

Permission policy example (Account B):

  {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Action": [
          "s3:GetObject",
          "s3:ListBucket"
        ],
        "Resource": [
          "arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket-from-account-b",
          "arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket-from-account-b/*"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }

Account A permission to assume the role:

  {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
        "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B_ID:role/CrossAccountS3AccessRole"
      }
    ]
  }

```text
Diagram :

  Account A (EC2 / IAM User) -> assumes role in Account B -> STS gives temporary credentials -> access S3 bucket in Account B

  Account A  ------------------->  Account B
  sts:AssumeRole               Role: CrossAccountS3AccessRole
      |                               |
      |                               | Trust policy allows Account A
      |                               |
      |------------ STS returns temporary credentials ------------>
      |                               |
   Access S3 bucket in Account B using temporary credentials

Key concept :

  - Account B owns the resource and creates the role.
  - Account B decides who is trusted through the trust policy.
  - Account B decides what actions are allowed through the permission policy.
  - Account A assumes the role using STS and gets temporary credentials.


